Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "WildlifeEncroachment" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasObstacle :obs1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :rain1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:actor1 a :Actor ;
    :description "Gorilla moving on roadway" .

:actor2 a :Actor ;
    :description "Elephant standing on road shoulder" .

:obs1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Large animal presence obstructing traffic lane" .

:rain1 a :RainyCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Potential collision with unpredictable wildlife on wet road" ;
    :confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Potential collision with unpredictable wildlife (gorilla and elephant) on a wet, rainy road surface.
Severity Score: 0.90